# Global Rules

Verify Config Signatures Rule:
Whenever configuring third-party providers (e.g. Firebase, Google Sign-In, Supabase), always automatically run local diagnostics (such as retrieving key fingerprints with keytool) to verify that the local Android/iOS build credentials perfectly match the remote configuration file specifications.

Automated Error Mapping Rule:
When designing seamless authentication screens (e.g. unified login/register entry points), always verify that all possible SDK exceptions (such as user-already-exists, wrong credentials, or rate limits) are explicitly mapped to specific user-friendly prompts rather than fallback default notices.

Cross-Device Theme Sync Rule:
When implementing or modifying theme/preference systems (e.g. mood themes, color accents, dark mode, reading themes), always auto-persist the user's selections to Supabase when authenticated, and restore them on login. Local SharedPreferences should serve as the fast cache, with Supabase as the source of truth for cross-device consistency.

# Strict Accessibility Targets
Ensure all interactive taps, buttons, or custom gesture triggers have a hit surface area of at least 44x44px. Custom gestures must specify `behavior: HitTestBehavior.opaque`.

# Zero-Latency Optimistic State Commits
Micro-interactions mutating server state (likes, flags, deletes) must commit immediately to memory or local cache before network requests, automatically rolling back only on absolute sync failure.

# Clean Separation via Design Tokens
Never hardcode raw hex values, border-radii, or layout padding in widget files. Color and style parameters must always query semantic bindings (`PremiumTokens` / theme configs) to maintain rebrand scalability.

# Recommended Rules:
- Ensure all notification configurations explicitly trigger the OS runtime permission requests (such as POST_NOTIFICATIONS for Android 13+) immediately on initialization or key user flows rather than assuming setup alone grants access.
- Prevent raw text emojis in interactive UI controls (tabs, filters, chips, status flags). Ensure emojis are split from labels and rendered using design-system vector icons via helper mappings.
- When resolving platform-specific plugins, check the locked package versions to target the exact classes (e.g., using `IOSFlutterLocalNotificationsPlugin` vs `DarwinFlutterLocalNotificationsPlugin`) to avoid compile failures.

